     "value": null
    },
    "FTL (°C)": {
     "choice": "measured",
     "probs": {
      "measured": 0.992,
      "literature": 0.008
     },
     "said": [
      "The thermal tolerances of common species were quanti-Wed in both Weld (foraging thermal limits, FTL) and laboratory (lethal temperatures, LT) settings; for a more detailed description of methods, see Wiescher et al.",
      "Using an infrared thermometer, FTL was measured as the mean surface temperature at which species would abandon resource baits (hot dog slices) in the Weld."
     ],
     "value": "measured"
    },
    "LT (°C)": {
     "said": [],
     "value": null
    },
    "AIWLR (mg × h-1× cm-2)": {
     "choice": "measured",
     "probs": {
      "measured": 0.927,
      "literature": 0.073
     },
     "said": [
      "Finally, we calculated area-independent water loss rates as: $\\mathrm{AIWLR} = (\\mathrm{WM} - \\mathrm{WC}) \\times (\\mathrm{LD50})^{-1} \\times (\\mathrm{SA})^{-1}$ This desiccation resistance measure enables across-species comparison by adjusting for surface area (Schilman et al.",
      "pergandei) were excluded from FTL, LT, and AIWLR experiments because we could not collect suYcient foragers."
     ],
     "value": "measured"
    }
   }
  },
  "3": {
   "long": false,
